# Records the exact window a migration was asked to move, written by `task migrate` and read by
# `task verify`. It describes one run of a throwaway lab, so it is local state, not source.
.migration-window

# Short-lived AWS session credentials, used only when driving a real migration over port-forward from a
# workstation. Never committed, and deleted as soon as the operation finishes.
.aws-creds.env

# Parameters for a real migration run (endpoints, filter, window). Local operational state describing one
# operator's run, not source.
.pilot.env

# Logs from real migration runs. Kept locally as an operational record — they name production namespaces,
# pod names and time windows, so they are not committed to a public lab repo.
.migration*.log

# A locally built migrator binary, if one is produced for a run outside the cluster.
.migrator-bin
